    {
      "id": "fr-sante-2",
      "title": "J'ai mal à la tête",
      "subtitle": "What hurts",
      "topics": [
        "health",
        "body"
      ],
      "words": [
        "health#I have a headache",
        "health#evil, harm",
        "health#health"
      ],
      "learn": [
        {
          "title": "avoir mal à",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "To say what hurts, use *avoir mal à* + article. Watch the contractions: *à + le = au*, *à + les = aux*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "textCols": [0],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "I have a headache.",
                  "J'ai mal à la tête."
                ],
                [
                  "I have a stomach ache.",
                  "J'ai mal au ventre."
                ],
                [
                  "My back hurts.",
                  "J'ai mal au dos."
                ],
                [
                  "I have a sore throat.",
                  "J'ai mal à la gorge."
                ],
                [
                  "My ear hurts.",
                  "J'ai mal à l'oreille."
                ],
                [
                  "I have toothache.",
                  "J'ai mal aux dents."
                ],
                [
                  "My legs hurt.",
                  "J'ai mal aux jambes."
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "cloze",
                "fr": "J'ai mal ___ ventre.",
                "a": [
                  "au"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Where does it hurt?",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "title": "it hurts = j'ai mal",
              "en": "In English the thing that hurts is often the subject (my head hurts); in French it's you: *J'ai mal* (literally \"I have pain\"). *Ma tête a mal* is wrong."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Questions: *Où est-ce que tu as mal ?* / *Où avez-vous mal ?* (Where does it hurt?) *Ça fait mal !* (That hurts!)"
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Tu as mal où ?",
                  "en": "Where does it hurt?"
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il a mal aux pieds après le match.",
                  "en": "His feet hurt after the match."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "J'ai très mal à la gorge.",
                  "en": "My throat really hurts."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Aïe, ça fait mal !",
                  "en": "Ouch, that hurts!"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "My back hurts.",
                "a": [
                  "J'ai mal au dos."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "vocab"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
